1
00:04:33,333 --> 00:04:39,333
Sleep Tight America. These Women Carry Guns.

2
00:09:06,666 --> 00:09:12,666
Feds! is a comedy, crime film directed by Daniel Goldberg.

3
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:46,000
Ellie DeWitt and Janis Zuckermann are admitted to
the very strict FBI Training Academy.

4
00:18:13,333 --> 00:18:19,333
They get a hard course, in which they learn to deal
with guns and to recognise crimes.

5
00:22:46,666 --> 00:22:52,666
They also get a physical training.

6
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:26,000
It appears that Ellie is a real fighting- machine, in
contrast with Janis, the great student.

7
00:31:53,333 --> 00:31:59,333
They have to help each other, all the way to graduation.

8
00:36:26,666 --> 00:36:32,666
Ellis DeWitt, played by Rebecca De Mornay.

9
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:06,000
Janis Zuckerman, played by Mary Gross.

10
00:45:33,333 --> 00:45:39,333
Bill Belecki, played by Fred Thompson.

11
00:50:06,666 --> 00:50:12,666
Howard Butz, played by Larry Cedar.

12
00:54:40,000 --> 00:54:46,000
Brent Sheppard, played by Ken Marshall.

13
00:59:13,333 --> 00:59:19,333
George Hupperman, played by Raymond Singer.

14
01:03:46,666 --> 01:03:52,666
Feds is a 1988 American crime comedy film co-written and directed by Dan
Goldberg, and starring Rebecca De Mornay and Mary Gross.

15
01:08:20,000 --> 01:08:26,000
The plot follows two women, the ex-Marine Ellie and Bryn Mawr graduate Janis, who aim
to become FBI agents and enroll at the training center in Quantico.

16
01:12:53,333 --> 01:12:59,333
The ending credits state that the real FBI did not support
the film or assist the production in any way.

17
01:17:26,666 --> 01:17:32,666
The tone is lighthearted.
